{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"1ac8e4203bad5600","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":1440,"height":810,"color":"5","label":"Execution tree • one possible shape"},
		{"id":"2ac8e4203bad5600","type":"group","x":1550,"y":0,"width":940,"height":810,"label":"Daemon • collection and acceptance"},
		{"id":"3ac8e4203bad5600","type":"group","x":1550,"y":910,"width":940,"height":320,"color":"6","label":"Convergence & continuation • sole leaf or in-tree summarizer"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f01","type":"text","text":"# TeamAgents execution tree\n\nEach round starts from the root (or previous sole leaf / summarizer). Blue arrows hand assignments downstream; a single leaf settles directly while 2+ leaves converge into an in-tree summarizer node.","x":0,"y":-320,"width":790,"height":180},
		{"id":"e70912d50e3f38fa","type":"text","text":"### Model selection\n\nUse ChatGPT via OAuth or an OpenAI-compatible API. In chat, `/model MODEL [EFFORT]` selects the model and reasoning effort for new tasks. Each root or continuation round saves its selection for workers, repair and reporting.","x":900,"y":-320,"width":540,"height":230},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f02","type":"text","text":"### Active subtree root\n\nRound 1 starts a fresh isolated session; continuation rounds promote the previous sole leaf or summarizer node to active root. Before acting it can ask via `answer ROOT_ID TEXT`.","x":50,"y":320,"width":350,"height":210,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f03","type":"text","text":"### Implementation stage\n\nCloses its stage and hands off two self-contained assignments in one transaction.","x":550,"y":140,"width":350,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f04","type":"text","text":"### Leaf • code\n\nImplements the requested change and records its result.","x":1040,"y":60,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f07","type":"text","text":"### Collect terminal leaves\n\nKeep leaf reports, stage IDs and outcomes. Active leaves coordinate via the per-root collaborative whiteboard (`wb_read`, `wb_write`, deadlock-free `wb_wait`). Each task retains its own detailed tool receipts.","x":1610,"y":310,"width":360,"height":200},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f0c","type":"text","text":"### Handoff and growth\n\nA handoff admits 1–64 children together with no session member cap. Member uniqueness is per round, allowing reuse across continuation rounds.","x":0,"y":930,"width":410,"height":250},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f0d","type":"text","text":"### Execution flow & limits\n\nReady turns and tools run concurrently without turn budgets or same-agent serialization. Shells default to direct bwrap workspace-write (opt-in `--staged`), paginate files >8 MiB, middle-truncate streams, allow `timeout_ms` up to 600s, auto-compact long histories, retry checks up to 10 attempts, and allow 5 action rejections (600s HTTP read timeout).","x":510,"y":930,"width":410,"height":250},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f0e","type":"text","text":"### Operation outcomes\n\nReview binds approvals to individual edits and shell commands. A started tool without a durable result has an unknown outcome and is never automatically replayed.","x":1020,"y":930,"width":410,"height":250},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f05","type":"text","text":"### Leaf • tests\n\nAdds coverage and records its result. Its parent stays closed.","x":1040,"y":320,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f06","type":"text","text":"### Leaf • documentation\n\nUpdates the usage example and records its result independently.","x":1040,"y":580,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f08","type":"text","text":"### Apply the root check\n\nA checked run needs a passing receipt for the exact submitted command. An unchecked run records `not_requested`.","x":1610,"y":580,"width":360,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f09","type":"text","text":"### Dispatch forward repair\n\nA failed check can start a fresh repair stage under the root. Its completion leads to another check. Ten attempts total.","x":2110,"y":580,"width":330,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f0a","type":"text","text":"### Sole leaf or in-tree summarizer\n\n1 terminal leaf settles directly at that leaf. 2+ terminal leaves spawn an in-tree `summarizer` node that writes the report with a read-only `whiteboard` snapshot and no workspace tools.","x":1610,"y":970,"width":360,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c40ac255312f1f0b","type":"text","text":"### User\n\nFollow-up input (`continue TASK_ID TEXT` or composer reply) promotes the sole leaf or summarizer node to the next round's subtree root.","x":2110,"y":970,"width":330,"height":200}
	],
